        "original_id": "17a02838-050d-5152-a47d-19f4fccf2724",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sangin, Lashkargah, Afghanistan, Sistan Basin\n- Systems: Helmand River, Route 611\n- Concepts: altitude, distance, watershed\n\nFacts:\n- The Helmand River is the longest river in Afghanistan and the primary watershed for the endorheic Sistan Basin.\n- Sangin is located in the valley of the Helmand River at an altitude of 888 meters.\n- Sangin is 95 kilometers northeast of Lashkargah.\n- Route 611 in Afghanistan is approximately 100 kilometers long.\n- Route 611 passes through the town of Sangin.",
